0212: 6-bit blend resolves that nothing would see are dropped

An EFB pass with blended RGBA6 draws is quantized (copy + full-screen pass) after it ends (0176).
When nothing in the pass reads its color afterwards (no color copy, no snapshot), the resolve now
waits for the next op: it runs before any op as before, except when that op is the next pass on
the same color target and clears its color completely (loadOp Clear, no pre-ops), where every
quantized pixel would be overwritten unseen; then it is dropped. In Luigi's Mansion that is the
shadow-map caster pass (rendered into the EFB, only its depth is copied) and similar passes ahead
of a full clear. A resolve still waiting at the end of the frame runs before the frame is
submitted. The picture is byte-identical. AURORA_EFB_BLEND6_NODEFER=1: resolve every pass (A/B).

